'''RTK111''' was a lawless [[Outer Rim Territories]] [[planet]]. It featured a [[city]] in a [[Warehouse district (Carnita arena)|warehouse district]] of which the [[Homeworld|native]] [[Abyssin]] [[gangster]] [[Gor Koresh]] ran the [[Gor Koresh's Honky Tonk]] illegal [[gladiator]] arena. In [[9 ABY]], the [[bounty hunter]] [[Din Djarin]] and the [[Yoda's species|alien]] [[youngling]] [[Din Grogu|Grogu]] visited the arena in order to meet Koresh. The gangster attempted to force Djarin to surrender his valuable [[Din Djarin's armor|Mandalorian armor]], which led to a fight. Djarin subsequently hung Koresh from a [[Lamp|streetlight]] outside the arena and then left him to fend off the local [[wild dog]] population.

==Description==
RTK111 was a terrestrial [[planet]]<ref name="SWE" /> located in grid square S-14 of the [[Standard Galactic Grid]] as part of the [[Outer Rim Territories]]<ref name="CL" /> and [[the Slice]].<ref name="Slice" /> It was part of an [[RTK111 system|eponymous star system]] in the [[Yminis sector]].<ref name="Appendix" /> A [[city]] on the planet<ref name="Insider210" /> featured [[Temperature|hot]] [[Atmosphere|air]]<ref name="Junior" /> and a population of [[wild dog]]s.<ref name="Art" />

==History==
{{Quote|I've been quested to bring ''[Grogu]'' to his kind. If I can locate other Mandalorians, they can help guide me. I'm told you know where to find them.''"<br />"''It's uncouth to talk business immediately. Just enjoy the entertainment.|Din Djarin and Gor Koresh|<ref name="Chapter 9" />}}
In [[9 ABY]],<ref name="Date">{{MandoDate|9}}</ref> the [[Mandalorian]] [[bounty hunter]] [[Din Djarin]] and the [[Yoda's species|alien]] [[youngling]] [[Din Grogu|Grogu]] traveled to a city on RTK111 in order to meet<ref name="Chapter 9" /> the [[Abyssin]] [[gangster]]<ref name="SWE" /> [[Gor Koresh]], who Djarin believed could help him located other Mandalorians. At [[Local day|night]], Djarin and [[Hover pram|hovering pram]]&ndash;riding Grogu traversed<ref name="Chapter 9" /> a backstreet alleyway<ref name="Junior" /> in a [[Warehouse district (Carnita arena)|warehouse district]]<ref name="Art" /> of the city to reach<ref name="Chapter 9" /> the illegal [[gladiator]] arena known as the [[Gor Koresh's Honky Tonk]].<ref name="SWE" /> There, the pair met with Koresh during a match between two [[Unidentified Gamorrean fighter 1|Gamorrean]] [[Unidentified Gamorrean fighter 2|gladiators]].<ref name="Chapter 9" />

[[File:DontLeaveMeHangin-TMCh9.png|thumb|right|300px|On RTK111, Din Djarin interrogated Gor Koresh after the gangster had attempted to take away his valuable armor.]]
Instead of helping Djarin, however, Koresh attempted to force him to surrender his valuable [[Din Djarin's armor|Mandalorian armor]], which led to the [[bounty]] [[Hunting|hunter]] defeating the gangster's underlings and chasing the Abyssin<ref name="Chapter 9" /> himself<ref name="SWE" /> in the alleyway outside. Djarin subsequently hanged Koresh upside down from a [[Lamp|streetlight]] and, after interrogating him for the information he was seeking, left the gangster at the mercy of the local wild [[dog]]s and departed RTK111.<ref name="Chapter 9" />

==Inhabitants==
{{Dialogue|Djarin|I'm here to see Gor Koresh.|Grogu|line2=no|[Coos.]|Doorman|Enjoy the fights.|attr=Din Djarin, Grogu, and a [[Unidentified Twi'lek doorman|Twi'lek doorman]]|src=<ref name="Chapter 9" />}}
A lawless world,<ref name="DB Koresh">{{Databank|gor-koresh|Gor Koresh}}</ref> RTK111 was the [[homeworld]] of the Abyssin gangster Gor Koresh.<ref name="SWE" /> Individuals of [[species]]<ref name="Chapter 9" /> from all over [[the galaxy]] attended the illegal gladiator matches at Gor Koresh's Honky Tonk that was run by the gangster.<ref name="SWE" />

==Locations==
{{Quote|You know this is no place for a child.|Gor Koresh, to Din Djarin while at Gor Koresh's Honky Tonk|<ref name="Chapter 9" />}}
A barren city was located on RTK111.<ref name="Insider210" /> It was the site of a warehouse district<ref name="Art" /> that also featured slums.<ref name="Junior" /> Gor Koresh's Honky Tonk was situated in the warehouse district.<ref name="Chapter 9" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:DawnOfRebellionGuide-Final.png|thumb|right|250px|''Star Wars: Dawn of Rebellion: The Visual Guide'' introduced RTK111's name.]]
The location that would eventually be identified as RTK111 first appeared in in "[[Chapter 9: The Marshal]],"<ref name="Chapter 9" /> the first episode of the [[Disney+]] television show ''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian]]''{{'s}} [[The Mandalorian Season Two|second season]]. The episode aired on [[October 30]], [[2020]].<ref name="Companion">{{InsiderCite|202|Star Wars: The Mandalorian Season Two Companion|''Star Wars: The Mandalorian'' Season Two Companion}}</ref> The concept supervisors [[Christian Alzmann]] and [[Erik Tiemens]] and concept artist [[Khang Le]] all provided concept art depicting the episode's exterior shots of that location.<ref name="Art" /> Before its debut in "Chapter 9: The Marshal," the location was featured in a trailer for ''The Mandalorian'' Season Two, which was released on the official ''[[Star Wars]]'' [https://www.youtube.com/c/StarWars YouTube channel] on [[September 15]], 2020.<ref name="Trailer">{{SWYouTube|eW7Twd85m2g|The Mandalorian &#124; Season 2 Official Trailer &#124; Disney+|sw_url=video/the-mandalorian-season-2-official-trailer}}</ref>

[[JAKe]]'s article "[[The Force of Beats and Rhymes]]" in<ref name="Insider201">{{InsiderCite|201|The Force of Beats and Rhymes}}</ref> the [[March 30]], [[2021]]<ref name="Titan">{{TitanComics|url=m/68-star-wars-insider-201|text=Star Wars Insider #201}}</ref> [[Star Wars Insider 201|201st issue]] of the ''[[Star Wars Insider]]'' magazine identified the location as a planet but misidentified it as "Koresh."<ref name="Insider201" /> The [[2023]] reference book ''[[Star Wars: Dawn of Rebellion: The Visual Guide]]'' by [[Pablo Hidalgo]] and [[Emily Shkoukani]] subsequently introduced the celestial body "RTK111,"<ref name="DoR">''[[Star Wars: Dawn of Rebellion: The Visual Guide]]''</ref> and finally the [[2024]] ''[[Star Wars Encyclopedia: The Comprehensive Guide to the Star Wars Galaxy]]'' established that the name referred to the planet first shown in "Chapter 9: The Marshal."<ref name="SWE" />

